---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import StatBlock from '../../../components/StatBlock.astro';
import Badge from '../../../components/Badge.astro';

const stats = [
  { value: 'Up to 4.5x', label: 'More root biomass vs. untreated' },
  { value: 'Up to 5.4x', label: 'Water/nutrient extraction capacity vs. untreated' },
  { value: '+12.9%', label: 'Production' },
  { value: '+USD 5,768 / ha', label: 'Additional net benefit' },
  { value: '30.8', label: 'Benefit / investment ratio' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  slug="case-studies/roots"
  title="Greenhouse Trial Case Study — AKAI"
  description="Up to 4.5x more root biomass, measured before the plant ever showed it. Digital phenotyping in a controlled rose trial in Colombia."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <video
      class="hero__video"
      autoplay
      muted
      loop
      playsinline
      poster="/media/posters/roots.jpg"
      src="/media/roots.mp4"
    ></video>
    <div class="hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="hero__content">
      <div class="hero__location"><Badge tone="dark">Freedom var. roses, El Rosal, Cundinamarca, COLOMBIA</Badge></div>
      <h1 class="hero__headline">Commercial evaluation under greenhouse conditions</h1>
      <p class="hero__subhead">
        Detection of active root biomass and its impact on water and nutrient uptake and on production.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="role">
    <div class="role__box">
      <h2 class="role__label">AKAI's role</h2>
      <p class="role__body">
        A biostimulant developer needed to prove their product's effect on crop physiology under real greenhouse
        conditions. AKAI supplied the measurement layer — digital phenotyping to track what was actually happening
        inside the plant, not just what showed up at harvest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="details">
    <div class="details__col">
      <h2 class="details__label">The problem</h2>
      <p class="details__body">
        Greenhouse rose growers in Colombia operate high-value crops increasingly exposed to drought, heat, and
        salinity. Yield swings tied to this kind of abiotic stress are hard to manage reactively — by the time
        stress is visible, productivity is already lost.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="details__col">
      <h2 class="details__label">AKAI solution</h2>
      <p class="details__body">
        Monitoring physiological variables throughout the entire rose crop cycle made it possible to identify the
        real impact of an algae extract on each internal process of the plant, explaining the increase in
        production and quality. Identifying these behaviors in early stages allows sound decisions to be made with
        anticipation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="results">
    <h2 class="results__label">Results</h2>
    <StatBlock stats={stats} />

    <div class="charts">
      <figure class="charts__card">
        <h3 class="charts__title">Active root biomass (Cp — nF) over days after evaluation (DDE)</h3>
        <img
          src="/assets/charts/biomasa-radicular.png"
          alt="Line chart of active root biomass (Cp) against days after evaluation (DDE), comparing the conventional (untreated) curve with treatments T1 (4 l/ha) and T2 (8 l/ha); the treated curves diverge above the conventional curve early in the cycle, well before any visible difference above ground."
          width="1202"
          height="874"
        />
        <figcaption class="charts__caption">
          Treated plots (T1: 4 l/ha, T2: 8 l/ha) diverge from the conventional curve well before any visible
          difference above ground.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="charts__card">
        <h3 class="charts__title">Water and nutrient extraction (Cs — nF) over days after evaluation (DDE)</h3>
        <img
          src="/assets/charts/extraccion-agua-nutrientes.png"
          alt="Line chart of water and nutrient extraction capacity (Cs) against days after evaluation (DDE), comparing the conventional (untreated) curve with treatments T1 and T2; extraction capacity recovers earlier and peaks higher in the treated plots."
          width="1296"
          height="914"
        />
        <figcaption class="charts__caption">
          Uptake capacity recovers earlier and peaks higher in treated plots — the physiological driver behind the
          production gain.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p class="results__why">
      The result isn't just a stronger root system — it's proof that physiological change can be measured and
      forecast weeks before it shows up in yield. That's the same measurement layer AKAI applies across every
      project, from greenhouse trials to plantation-scale palm.
    </p>

    <div class="disclosure" data-disclosure>
      <button type="button" class="disclosure__trigger" data-disclosure-trigger aria-expanded="false"
        >Read the full story</button
      >
      <div class="disclosure__panel" data-disclosure-panel hidden>
        <p>
          The trial compared treated and untreated blocks across a full growth cycle, tracking root biomass,
          production, and downstream economics. AKAI's sensing pipeline surfaced the root-level divergence early,
          before it was visible in canopy or yield — giving growers a lead-time advantage on the decisions that
          mattered.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <a href="/en/contact/" class="results__cta">I WANT TO CONTACT THEM</a>
  </section>

  <div class="pagenav">
    <a href="/en/case-studies/palm/" class="pagenav__link">
      <span class="pagenav__arrow" aria-hidden="true">←</span>
      <span>Palm Case Study</span>
    </a>
    <a href="/en/" class="pagenav__link">
      <span class="pagenav__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
      <span>Back to top</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100vh;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-ink);
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
  }
  .hero__video {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    z-index: 0;
  }
  .hero__scrim {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 0%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2) 45%, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.72) 100%);
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .hero__content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    padding: 0 var(--section-padding-x) var(--space-14);
    max-width: 900px;
  }
  .hero__location {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }
  .hero__headline {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: var(--weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
  .hero__subhead {
    margin: 0;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
    font-size: var(--text-body-lg);
    max-width: 560px;
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .role {
    width: 100%;
    padding: var(--space-13) var(--section-padding-x) 0;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  .role__box {
    max-width: var(--content-max-width);
    width: 100%;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
    background: var(--color-neutral-100);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .role__label {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .role__body {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .details {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0 var(--section-padding-x);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-10);
    max-width: var(--content-max-width);
    margin: var(--space-11) auto 0;
  }
  .details__label {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .details__body {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .results {
    width: 100%;
    padding: var(--space-11) var(--section-padding-x) var(--space-9);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-7);
  }
  .results__label {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-widest);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .charts {
    max-width: var(--content-max-width);
    width: 100%;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(380px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }
  .charts__card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: var(--space-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-paper);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .charts__title {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }
  .charts__card img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .charts__caption {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--color-neutral-500);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .results__why {
    max-width: 680px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .disclosure {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }
  .disclosure__trigger {
    background: none;
    border: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .disclosure__panel p {
    max-width: 680px;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--text-body);
    color: var(--color-neutral-700);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .results__cta {
    display: inline-block;
    background: var(--color-ink);
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sharp);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
  }

  .pagenav {
    width: 100%;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--space-7);
    padding: var(--space-5) 0 var(--space-11);
  }
  .pagenav__link {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--text-small);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
  }
  .pagenav__arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 18px;
    transform: translateY(1px);
  }
</style>
